<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Celulosa denies sale rumors.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Celulosa denies sale rumors.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine pulp and paper maker Celulosa Friday denied market rumors of a possible buyout by a leading U.S. company.</p>
<p>&quot;There's no such thing,&quot; spokesman Omar Fernandez Suarez told Reuters. &quot;There's simply stronger domestic sales in paper for printing and writing and exports have also recovered.&quot;</p>
<p>Celulosa shares surged 15 percent Friday before Suarez spoke, but slashed gains to just 1.0 percent at the close. It gained 27 percent in the week.</p>
<p>((--Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom 541 318-0650))</p>
